    "## 9. Training\n",
    "\n",
    "The model is trained using a standard PyTorch training loop with the following configuration:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Device:** MPS (Apple Silicon) if available, otherwise CPU. For Windows, switch to the CUDA line.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hyperparameters:**\n",
    "- Epochs: 10 (may stop earlier via Early Stopping)\n",
    "- Batch size: 32\n",
    "- Learning rate: 0.0001\n",
    "\n",
    "**Loss & Optimizer:** CrossEntropyLoss for binary classification, Adam optimizer for weight updates.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Learning Rate Scheduler (`ReduceLROnPlateau`):**  \n",
    "Monitors validation loss each epoch. If it does not improve for 2 consecutive epochs, the learning rate is halved (factor=0.5). This prevents the model from overshooting the optimum.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Early Stopping:**  \n",
    "If the validation loss does not improve for 3 consecutive epochs, training is halted and the best model weights are restored. This avoids overfitting and unnecessary computation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Training Loop (per epoch):**\n",
    "1. Forward pass → compute loss\n",
    "2. Backward pass → update weights\n",
    "3. Evaluate on validation set (no gradient computation)\n",
    "4. Scheduler step based on validation loss\n",
    "5. Early stopping check"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0051e571",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
